{1 Guides}

- {{:https://github.com/thevilledev/ocaml-ohttp/blob/main/doc/getting-started.md}Getting started}: installation and the runnable example.
- {{:https://github.com/thevilledev/ocaml-ohttp/blob/main/doc/http-libraries.md}HTTP libraries}: carrying the messages with cohttp, or with anything else.
- {{:https://github.com/thevilledev/ocaml-ohttp/blob/main/doc/protocol-support.md}Protocol support}: features, algorithms, and known gaps.
- {{:https://github.com/thevilledev/ocaml-ohttp/blob/main/doc/interoperability.md}Interoperability}: how other implementations compare.
- {{:https://github.com/thevilledev/ocaml-ohttp/blob/main/doc/development.md}Development}: building, testing, and the module map.
- {{:https://github.com/thevilledev/ocaml-ohttp/blob/main/doc/releasing.md}Release checklist}: preparing and validating the opam packages.

These guides are also installed as Markdown under the package's documentation
directory.

{1 Security}

See the repository's
{{:https://github.com/thevilledev/ocaml-ohttp/blob/main/SECURITY.md}security policy}
for what the library checks, what it leaves to applications, its known
limitations, and private vulnerability reporting.
